From 58200afcbc660e6070d95052fb161076da86787c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 05:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add sourced evidence modules to industry pages, fix imprecise
 source links, dedupe homepage stat, add contact intake field

Implements the priority items from the reconciled website audit (original + external review):

- Add "What has been reported" evidence sections to all five industry pages,
  distinguishing verified reported cases (amber label) from labelled
  hypothetical scenarios (teal label), each with a source + date + why-it's-here line:
  - Healthcare: Ontario IPC medical imaging clinic ransomware case study (2024)
  - Professional Services: CAFC-recovered $2.3M law firm BEC case (2025) +
    document-verification scenario
  - Retail & Hospitality: Canada Computers & Electronics breach (2025-2026) +
    QR-menu integrity scenario
  - Construction: documented Competition Bureau fraud pattern + unexpected-
    document scenario (no off-industry case implied as construction-specific)
  - Property Management: scenario-only, no incident citation until a
    genuinely on-point Canadian source is found
- Fix source links that pointed to organization homepages instead of the
  specific relevant pages (IPC handbook + case study, Law Society of Ontario
  cybersecurity/fraud page, Retail Council's Retail CyberSecure program)
- Remove the homepage's duplicated cyber-incident statistic (kept the fuller,
  better-sourced four-stat strip; removed the standalone repeat)
- Add a multi-select "which parts of your business" contact-form field as a
  more precise alternative to any generic privacy question

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M6rgfCRoJqp3MGgw2zonvp
